-- Resources content for Sourcework: every guide checked against the tool as it is on 2026-10-15
-- and rewritten where it had drifted (CLAUDE.md, "Resources stay in step with the code").
-- Content only; no schema. Depends on 20261102130000.
--
-- Three things to know about this file:
--
-- 1. The version prefix continues the sequence of the already-applied files, which ran ahead of
--    the calendar (20261016… through 20261102… were written and applied between 2026-10-09 and
--    2026-10-15). It is a sequence number, not a date; the real dates are in APPLIED.md. A new
--    migration must still sort after every applied one, or a fresh database would run it first
--    and the older files would overwrite what it writes.
--
-- 2. The release notes those files wrote took their released_on from the filename, so What's new
--    showed changes dated up to 2026-11-01 in mid-October. The updates below set each one to the
--    day the change reached production, from APPLIED.md. Slugs keep their original names: a slug
--    is the identity rc_release_note() matches on, nothing shows it to a reader, and renaming
--    would make the older migrations re-create the old rows on a fresh database.
--
-- 3. Two guide versions existed only in production, written there directly on 2026-10-10 with no
--    migration: a "From interview recording to radio script" walkthrough
--    (sourcework-interview-to-script) and a fifth version of the workflow overview. Both are
--    brought into the repository here, corrected, so the repository is the source of truth again;
--    on preview the walkthrough is created for the first time.
--
-- What changed on screen since the guides were last written, and is reflected below: the home
-- page's Source library and All excerpts became one Notebook tab with one search box; the project
-- screen has no transcript or source switcher (a source is its own screen) and its tabs are
-- Notebook (Sources, Data points, Excerpts), Review, Synthesis, Pieces and Setup; Delete project
-- is in the ⋮ menu; the editors' pages are the Setup tab (Prompts, with a fourth Writing guide,
-- and Piece formats); themes, theme quotes and Draft with AI are gone and clips Analyze proposes
-- are decided on the Review tab or the source's page; the step strip is left out on a phone and
-- once the project has a piece.

update public.rc_articles set released_on = '2026-10-09' where slug = 'release-2026-10-11-sourcework-pieces' and kind = 'release_note';
update public.rc_articles set released_on = '2026-10-10' where slug = 'release-2026-10-12-sourcework-research' and kind = 'release_note';
update public.rc_articles set released_on = '2026-10-10' where slug = 'release-2026-10-13-sourcework-themes' and kind = 'release_note';
